while plenty of your favorite movies  actually get the critical acclaim and  box-office success they deserve there  are some amazing films that just don't  seem to click with an audience still  just because a film wasn't a box-office  success at first release doesn't mean  that it's not worth your time here are  some genuinely great movies from this  decade that bombed at the box office  free fire British director Ben Wheatley  who made the modern horror masterpiece  kill list  quietly dropped free fire in 2017 hardly  anybody saw it but free fire has got all  the makings of a cult classic the film  is a lean romp that takes place almost  entirely inside a single warehouse free  fire tells the story of an arms deal  gone wrong leaving all the lowlifes  involved trapped with nothing but their  wits and a whole lot of guns to get them  out it's filled with offbeat humor  one-liners and physical comedy that  nicely breaks the tension here and there  hey Burt does everybody like you where  you come from Fitri de mysteriis chul  Tomorrowland a fun exuberant and  inventive science fiction tale  Tomorrowland was one of the better  science fiction films of the last ten  years the film features George Clooney  as a reclusive genius inventor who meets  a science crazed teenage girl their  adventures center around Tomorrowland an  alternate dimension of scientific wonder  full of twists turns and some compelling  sci-fi concepts under director Brad  Birds expert direction  Tomorrowland deserved to be a huge hit  Scott Pilgrim vs. the world there are  movies that fail at the box office that  are only guilty of being released a few  years too early and it was clear from  the first trailer that Scott Pilgrim vs.  the world was ahead of its time director  Edgar Wright chose to ramp up the comic  book and video game influence on the  story all the way to 11 bad guys explode  in piles of coins and sound effects  appear written out on the screen  it's a self-aware and self referential  film winking at the audience constantly  and packed to the gills with nostalgia  for classic video games if released in  today's age of metatextual pop culture  the film probably would have been a  massive success hi big fan why wouldn't  you be pop star never stopped never  stopping a fake documentary spoofing  concert biopics of modern pop sensations  should be a one-note journey with a few  good jabs about Instagram culture and  auto-tune at best  instead pop star never stopped never  stopping turned into one of the best  mainstream comedies of 2016 created by  comedy music group The Lonely Island the  film stars Andy Samberg as Connor a  Justin Bieber ask pop star on the rise  it's got plenty of laughs but what's  more surprising is how much heart is  hidden beneath its many celebrity cameos  unfortunately it underperformed at the  box office but we think time is going to  be kind to this one Dredd lean  relentless and running at a breakneck  pace Dredd is a viscerally satisfying  sci-fi action film adapted from the  long-running British comic series Judge  Dredd the film sees future super cop  Judge Dredd and his trainee judge  Anderson trapped in a massive skyscraper  with hundreds of armed thugs out to kill  him leading the gang of criminals is  mama a notorious drug dealer played with  ruthless relish by Game of Thrones Lena  Headey the film is a violent brutal romp  taking Dredd and Anderson up through the  buildings many floors in increasingly  inventive action sequences  Pannalal premium rush an action crime  story set in the world of fixed-gear  bike messengers shouldn't work and yet  somehow premium rush is fantastic  premium rush is anchored by the  excellent Michael Shannon who really  shines in his role as a crooked cop as  he relentlessly pursues Joseph  gordon-levitt's bike messenger character  throughout New York City the film  showcases some killer chase sequences  and well edited action scenes the film's  nonlinear narrative seals the deal  making premium rush a whole lot of fun  and very much worth your time warrior  the story of two brothers separated as  teenagers who find themselves forced to  fight one another in a mixed martial  arts tournament sounds cliche at first  glance but warrior is surprisingly  powerful the brothers played by Joel  Edgerton and Tom Hardy have gone down  separate paths since their separation  but are perpetually tied together by  their alcoholic screw-up father warrior  is very much rocky for the UFC  generation and the movie packs the same  emotional punch of Sylvester Stallone  seminal classic this is one you  shouldn't miss but make sure you bring  tissues you'll need them you're not the  only one who suffered Tommy's  I didn't even know she was Shaykh  [Music]
 

